      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T06:53:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the bug (b:279522279) you say `cc off` should emulate DUT-side disconnect.  I agree with that, within the confines of the current `cc` interface.\n\nInstead of this, what if we changed `cc off` to remove `CC_EMCA_SERVO`, and changed the other `cc` subcommands to add it back?  (Leaving `cc emca` and `cc noemca` unchanged.)\n\nWe should really revisit the `cc` interface as a whole (b:248383961).",
      "revId": "24b8789bebaeed7fed5d96b36d2d68bfdc90ff95",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c8b47f69_598ead5a",
        "filename": "board/servo_v4p1/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 573,
      "author": {
        "id": 1269501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-24T19:38:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Instead of this, what if we changed cc off to remove CC_EMCA_SERVO, and changed the other cc subcommands to add it back? \n\nCC_EMCA_SERVO is merely a (stateful) configuration tracking bit.  \nWiping it would only wipe the variable tracking user setting.\n\n\u003e We should really revisit the cc interface as a whole (b:248383961).\n\nAgreed. Command params doesn\u0027t indicate \u0027PD\u0027 usage; it\u0027s completely legacy.  \nIn my (abandoned) WIP refactor, I split all commands to be grammatically correct.\n\nExample: \"cc [?:PD][SNK|SRC][?:DTS] [?:cc1|cc2] for all 2*2*2 variants.  \nAnd further adding either a separate param/command to set Rp signal level.  \n(Which is completely not possible right now.)",
      "parentUuid": "61cfc536_45233834",
      "revId": "24b8789bebaeed7fed5d96b36d2d68bfdc90ff95",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ffb65643_11c75dbf",
        "filename": "board/servo_v4p1/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 583,
